@startuml d8-replication
title D8 - Asynchronous live WAL shipping; bootstrap is separate
participant "Master: FlushCommandsToWAL\n(wal.go:317)" as MW
participant "replication.Sender" as SND
participant "GRPCReplicationServer\nGetWALStream (grpc_server.go:42)" as GS
participant "Replica: Receiver.Run\n(receiver.go:34)" as RCV
participant "ReplayerImpl.Replay\n(replay.go:38)" as RP
participant "Replica writer\n(default writer)" as RW
RCV -> GS : GetWALStream() at startup / retryable reconnect
note over GS,RCV
  New subscriber channel: subsequent broadcasts only.
  No initial snapshot, historical cursor or remote-commit ACK.
  EOF and replay errors stop; other receive/connect errors retry.
end note
MW -> SND : Send(TG bytes) after WAL fsync
note over SND
  Send queues locally; no remote commit wait.
  Bounded queues, 500 groups each: the sender queue (sender.go:11)
  and each replica stream channel (grpc_server.go:15).
  A full replica channel blocks the fan-out (grpc_server.go:83),
  then Send, then the master flush.
  The channel map has no lock (grpc_server.go:52, 72, 81).
  A failed stream closes its channel (grpc_server.go:73) while the
  fan-out may be sending on it: the send panics, the master stops.
  Read from the code; no race detector or crash test was run.
end note
SND -> GS : SendReplicationMessage(TG)
GS -> RCV : stream.Send(TransactionGroup)
RCV -> RP : Replay(TG)
RP -> RW : ParseTGData -> WTSet -> ColumnSeriesMap -> WriteCSM
note over RW
  HTTP Write uses injected ErrorWriter on replicas.
  gRPC Write bypasses it via global executor.WriteCSM.
  SQL INSERT INTO via Query (HTTP or gRPC) does too.
  Create/Destroy mutate the catalog without this guard.
  Deletes are not replicated; bootstrap/gap repair is external.
end note
@enduml
